{title: Bless the LORD, O My Soul}
{subtitle: Psalm 103}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 96}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Abmaj7/C] [Bb] [Ab] [Eb/G] |
| [Fm7] [Bb7sus4] |

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Bless the LORD, my [Bb]soul;
all that is with[Cm7]in me, bless his [Ab]holy name.
[Eb]Bless the LORD, my [Bb]soul, and do not [Cm7]forget all his ben[Ab]e[Eb]fits—
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
he forgives all your [Bb]sin and heals all your diseases;
[Cm]he redeems your life from the pit and crowns [Ab]you with steadfast love and mer[Eb]cy;
he satisfies you with good as long as [Bb]you live, so your youth is [Ab]renewed like [Eb/G]the eagle's.
The [Fm7]LORD does what is right and brings jus[Ab]tice to all who are op[Bbsus4]pressed.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He made known his [Eb]ways to Moses, his deeds to the people of Is[Bb]rael.
The LORD is merciful and gracious, slow [Cm]to anger and abounding in steadfast [Ab]love.
He will not always accuse, nor [Eb]hold his anger forever.
He [Bb]does not treat us as our sins [Cm]deserve or repay [Ab]us accord[Eb]ing to our guilt.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
For as high [Bb]as the heavens are above [Ab]the earth, so great is his steadfast love [Eb]toward those who fear him.
As far as the east is from the west, [Bb]so far has he re[Cm]moved our transgressions from us.
[Ab]As a father has [Eb]compassion on his children, so the [Bb]LORD has compassion on those [Cm]who fear him.
For [Ab]he knows how we are formed;
[Eb]he remembers that we are dust.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
As [Bb]for man, his days [Cm]are like grass;
he blooms like a flow[Ab]er of the field—
for [Eb]the wind passes o[Bb]ver it, and [Ab]it is gone, and its place [Eb]knows it no more.
[Eb]But the steadfast love of [Bb]the LORD rests from everlasting to ev[Cm]erlasting on those who [Ab]fear him, and his [Eb]righteousness on their children's [Bb]children—
to those who [Cm]keep his covenant and remember to o[Ab]bey his precepts.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
The [Eb]LORD has established his throne in the heav[Bb]ens, and his [Ab]kingdom rules over [Eb]all.
Bless the LORD, you his angels, you mighty ones [Bb]who do his word, o[Cm]beying the voice of his [Ab]word.
Bless the LORD, [Eb]all his hosts, you his servants [Bb]who do his will.
Bless the LORD, [Cm]all his works, in every place of [Ab]his dominion.
Bless the LORD, [Eb]my [Bb]soul.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Bless the [Cm]LORD, my [Ab]soul; [Eb]
[Bb]all that is with[Cm]in me, bless his [Ab]holy name.
